 "critic": "Most fragments omit the actual act, subject, motive or requested help, so named participants rarely become distinct people. Explicit causal pointers sometimes assert connections without explaining them. Requests to act against the asker remain unexplained. Closing labels such as protection or resolved do not show what changed. Concrete paid jobs provide clear actions and practical motives, but instant completion hides decisions and consequences. Repeated plots with changed names dominate. Night City detail is concentrated in currency, gangs and a few props. The refusal prompting someone else to help offers the strongest glimpse of lives continuing beyond the protagonist."
